# SPI Overview

## What is SPI?

SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface) is a synchronous serial communication protocol commonly used to communicate between a controller and peripheral devices.

Unlike UART, SPI uses a clock signal generated by the master to synchronize communication.

## SPI Signals

The basic SPI interface consists of four signals:

| Signal | Name |          Direction           |
|--------|------|------------------------------|
| SCLK | Serial Clock |     Master → Slave     |
| MOSI | Master Out, Slave In | Master → Slave |
| MISO | Master In, Slave Out | Slave → Master |
| CS | Chip Select |       Master → Slave      |

## Architecture


