# SPI Communication

SPI transfers data one bit at a time.

For an 8-bit transfer:

Master → Slave

D7 → D6 → D5 → D4 → D3 → D2 → D1 → D0

At the same time, the slave can send data back to the master through MISO.

This means SPI is full-duplex.

MOSI:  D7 → D6 → D5 → D4 → D3 → D2 → D1 → D0
MISO:  D7 ← D6 ← D5 ← D4 ← D3 ← D2 ← D1 ← D0

