# Part 1 – SPI Master

## Goal

Implement an SPI master capable of generating the SPI clock and controlling the communication with a slave device.

## Responsibilities

The master controls:

- SCLK
- MOSI
- CS

The master receives:

- MISO

## Concepts Learned

- SPI master
- Serial clock generation
- Chip select
- MOSI
- MISO
- Serial data transmission
- Full-duplex communication

## Reflection

The SPI master introduced synchronous serial communication.

Unlike UART, where the communicating devices must agree on a baud rate, SPI uses a clock generated by the master to synchronize the transfer.

The master therefore controls when data is transmitted and received.

## Problems

The main challenge was making sure that the data was shifted and sampled on the correct clock edge.

Careful inspection of the simulation waveform was used to verify the timing of SCLK, MOSI, MISO and CS.

---

# Part 2 – SPI Slave

## Goal

Implement an SPI slave capable of receiving and transmitting data synchronized to the master's clock.

## Responsibilities

The slave receives:

- SCLK
- MOSI
- CS

The slave generates:

- MISO

## Concepts Learned

- SPI slave
- Clocked data reception
- Serial-to-parallel conversion
- Parallel-to-serial conversion
- Chip select handling

## Reflection

The SPI slave demonstrated how a peripheral can synchronize its operation to an externally generated clock.

The chip select signal determines when the slave should participate in communication.

## Problems

The main challenge was ensuring that the slave shifted and sampled data at the correct clock edges.

